{"key":"enterprise/T1558","id":"T1558","name":"Steal or Forge Kerberos Tickets","domain":"enterprise","level":"technique","parent_id":null,"tactics":["credential-access"],"platforms":["Linux","macOS","Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may attempt to subvert Kerberos authentication by stealing or forging Kerberos tickets to enable Pass the Ticket. Kerberos is an authentication protocol widely used in modern Windows domain environments. In Kerberos environments, referred to as “realms”, there are three basic participants: client, service, and Key Distribution Center (KDC). Clients request access to a service and through the exchange of Kerberos tickets, originating…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1558","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--3fc01293-ef5e-41c6-86ce-61f10706b64a","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.628Z","source_object_version":"1.7","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0084","name":"Active Directory Credential Request","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0084","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--02d090b6-8157-48da-98a2-517f7edd49fc","page":"telemetry/DC0084/"},{"id":"DC0055","name":"File Access","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0055","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--235b7491-2d2b-4617-9a52-3c0783680f71","page":"telemetry/DC0055/"},{"id":"DC0088","name":"Logon Session Metadata","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0088","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--39b9db72-8b48-4595-a18d-db5bbba3091b","page":"telemetry/DC0088/"},{"id":"DC0035","name":"Process Access","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0035","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--1887a270-576a-4049-84de-ef746b2572d6","page":"telemetry/DC0035/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0522","name":"Detect Kerberos Ticket Theft or Forgery (T1558)","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0522","stix_id":